WEBVTT

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:43.000
ALHAMDU LILLAAH, We praise God

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:47.000
WA ASHHADU AN LA ILLAAHA ILLAA ALLAH, WAHDAHU LAA SHARIKA LAH

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:50.000
And we bear witness that there is no god except the One God.

00:02:50.000 --> 00:02:57.000
It is very important for any person to know who God is

00:02:57.000 --> 00:03:02.000
to really appreciate why millions of people fall into idol worship.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:14.000
Why do they leave God and idolize Muhammad, or Jesus, or Marry or St. Francis or St. Jude or some helpless creature?

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:21.000
And the main reason is that the people do not know who God is. They do not appreciate the greatness of God.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:29.000
So, my purpose in this sermon is to share with you some idea about the greatness of God.

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:38.000
And to appreciate the greatness of God, we have to think of this universe that we are living in.

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.000
Our planet earth is part of the solar system, as you all know.

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:49.000
And by the way, I'm gonna talk to you strictly about scientific facts,

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.000
established scientific facts.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.000
This earth is part of the solar system.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.000
It is the only planet in the solar system that has life.

00:04:01.000 --> 00:04:07.000
We went to the moon and we didn't see a single tree there or a mouse, nothing.

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:11.000
We sent cameras to Mars and we didn't see a creature there

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:16.000
unless those rocks are creatures, as we saw in one of the cartoons.

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:20.000
There is no life in the solar system except here, on the planet Earth,

00:04:20.000 --> 00:04:30.000
Our Sun, the center of this solar system is 93 million miles away.

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.000
Now, I want you to watch these distances.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:38.000
93 million miles away from us, the Sun.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:42.000
And the light comes to us from the Sun in 4 minutes.

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.000
So, remember this relationship.

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:51.000
The light travels from the Sun to the Earth 93 million miles in 4 minutes.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:05:01.000
The solar system itself spans a distance of 2 billion to 4 billion miles.

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:03.000
This is our solar system.

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:15.000
So, when you go to the edge of our solar system, if you travel 2 billion, with a b, 2 billion miles away,

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:17.000
how big is the planet Earth, from that point?

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:20.000
It will seem small.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.000
OK. Let us now go a little further.

00:05:23.000 --> 00:05:26.000
Let us talk about the galaxy, our galaxy.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.000
As you know, it is called the Milky way galaxy.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:43.000
And the solar system is one... the Sun of the solar system is one of one billion suns or stars in our Milky way galaxy.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:53.000
It will take 4 minutes for the light to travel from the Sun to the planet Earth, 93 million miles.

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:58.000
You know how long it will take to cross the Milky way galaxy?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:09.000
If you travel at the speed of light, you will cross the Milky way galaxy, our galaxy, in 100,000 years.

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:16.000
Not 4 minutes, or 10 minutes or 1 hour or 10 hours or 10 days or 10 years.

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:26.000
It will take you 100,000 years to travel across the Milky way galaxy, our galaxy.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:34.000
Now, so, if you go to the border, the edge of the Milky way galaxy and try to find the planet Earth, where is it?

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.000
It is minute. Isn't it?

00:06:36.000 --> 00:06:38.000
Just a tiny mote.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.000
You know, when you look at the Sunlight and see these little things flying,

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.000
those are called motes.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:50.000
And the Earth is not even that within the Milky way galaxy.

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.000
Well, let us travel. Let us go on a little further.

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:59.000
Let us go to our next door galaxy, our neighbor.

00:06:59.000 --> 00:07:02.000
You know how far it is, our neighbor galaxy?

00:07:02.000 --> 00:07:07.000
2 million light years away.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:17.000
So, if you're cooking something and you wanna borrow some salt or some sugar from your neighbors, don't go to the next door galaxy.

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:24.000
It will take you 2 million years going at the speed of light, and 2 million years coming at the speed of light

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:27.000
and your cooking will be all gone.

00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:37.000
So, 2 million light years from our galaxy to the next door galaxy.

00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:46.000
Now, so, if you go to the next door galaxy and try to find the planet Earth in the Milky way,

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:50.000
how... what are your chances of seeing the planet Earth?

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:54.000
Using the strongest, possible, imaginable telescope,

00:07:54.000 --> 00:07:56.000
can you find the planet Earth?

00:07:56.000 --> 00:08:03.000
How about your house? Or you? Or any human being, like Jesus or Muhammad?

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:08.000
Can you see them from that galaxy, our next door galaxy?

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:13.000
Shall we move a little further?

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:20.000
There are one billion galaxies in our universe.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:23.000
This is one billion with a b.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.000
A billion trillion stars in our galaxy

00:08:31.000 --> 00:08:34.000
in our universe, excuse me.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:37.000
There are one billion galaxies in our universe.

00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:42.000
A billion trillion stars in our universe.

00:08:44.000 --> 00:08:55.000
Our universe now has distances of 10, 15, up to 26 billion light years, distances within our universe.

00:08:55.000 --> 00:09:00.000
And you can easily imagine this now. If our next door galaxy...

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:06.000
And these are all, I remind you, these are all scientific, established scientific facts.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:14.000
26 billion light years within our universe.

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:21.000
You have to agree with me that when you go to the edge of our universe,

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:28.000
It is hopeless to try to find the planet earth.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:33.000
It is such an insignificant spec in God's kingdom.

00:09:36.000 --> 00:09:43.000
It is an established physical fact that when you go, if you go to the edge of our universe,

00:09:43.000 --> 00:09:53.000
you cannot possibly see the planet Earth. You cannot possibly see the Sun of our solar system, let alone the planet Earth.

00:09:54.000 --> 00:09:56.000
So that's our universe.

00:09:56.000 --> 00:010:00.000
Before we leave our universe, that's the next step,

00:010:00.000 --> 00:010:10.000
I would like to remind you that, in fact, I will do a calculation thing with you right now.

00:010:10.000 --> 00:010:16.000
Let us say the number of stars in our universe is not a billion trillion.

00:010:16.000 --> 00:010:19.000
Let us just take a smaller number, quintillion.

00:010:19.000 --> 00:010:21.000
Quintillion.

00:010:21.000 --> 00:010:24.000
That's a smaller number of stars in our universe.

00:010:24.000 --> 00:010:33.000
And let us count from one to quintillion, taking one second per count.

00:010:33.000 --> 00:010:39.000
It's like... let us say, we're counting the stars: one, two, three, four, ...

00:010:39.000 --> 00:010:41.000
one second per count.

00:010:41.000 --> 00:010:44.000
So, you take one quintillion, divide by sixty,

00:010:44.000 --> 00:010:50.000
you get the number of minutes it will take you to count from one to quintillion.

00:010:50.000 --> 00:010:54.000
Then, you take this number and divide it by sixty, again,

00:010:54.000 --> 00:010:59.000
you get the number of hours it will take us to count from one to quintillion.

00:010:59.000 --> 00:011:03.000
Now, we take this last product and divide by 24,

00:011:03.000 --> 00:011:11.000
and you get the number of days it will take you to count from one to quintillion.

00:011:12.000 --> 00:011:14.000
These are physical facts

00:011:14.000 --> 00:011:19.000
as you see, just a simply dividing by the seconds, the minutes, the hours and the days.

00:011:19.000 --> 00:011:22.000
Divide by 7, you get the number of weeks.

00:011:22.000 --> 00:011:25.000
Then, you divide by 4, you get the number of months.

00:011:25.000 --> 00:011:33.000
Divide by 12, you get the number of years, it will take you to count, just count a quintillion stars.

00:011:33.000 --> 00:011:37.000
You know how long it will take you? How many years?

00:011:37.000 --> 00:011:40.000
This is a mathematical physical fact.

00:011:40.000 --> 00:011:52.000
It will take you 32 billion with a b, 32 billion years, just to count a quintillion stars in our universe.

00:011:52.000 --> 00:011:55.000
And God created them.

00:011:55.000 --> 00:012:00.000
God didn't just count them. God created them.

00:012:00.000 --> 00:012:04.000
And we are talking only about stars in our universe.

00:012:04.000 --> 00:012:07.000
We're not talking about the planets that go with those stars.

00:012:07.000 --> 00:012:18.000
We're not talking about the uncountable decillions of heavenly bodies and meteorites that are in our universe.

00:012:18.000 --> 00:012:20.000
We're talking only about stars.

00:012:20.000 --> 00:012:24.000
The Sun is one of the stars, our Sun.

00:012:24.000 --> 00:012:29.000
By the way, it is one of the dim stars.

00:012:29.000 --> 00:012:42.000
The bright stars, the definition of a bright star is it must be at least one million times as bright as our Sun.

00:012:42.000 --> 00:012:44.000
Look outside and see how bright the Sun is.

00:012:44.000 --> 00:012:52.000
A bright star has to be a million times as bright as this, as our Sun

00:012:52.000 --> 00:012:59.000
We had a conference here at the University of Arizona that dealt with bright stars only

00:013:00.000 --> 00:013:01.000
and the Sun was not one of them

00:013:01.000 --> 00:013:06.000
because by definition a bright star is a million times as bright as our Sun.

00:013:06.000 --> 00:013:18.000
So, it will take you 32 billion years just to count, not to create, just to count a quintillion of the billion trillion stars we have in our universe.

00:013:18.000 --> 00:013:19.000
That's our universe.

00:013:19.000 --> 00:013:22.000
Now, prepare for a shock.

00:013:22.000 --> 00:013:34.000
This universe, our universe, vast as we can imagine is only one of seven universes.

00:013:34.000 --> 00:013:40.000
And it is the smallest and innermost of the seven universes.

00:013:40.000 --> 00:013:47.000
This is a fact that is in the Quran proven by the Quran's mathematical code.

00:013:47.000 --> 00:013:54.000
We are all now familiar with the Mathematical code of the Quran that prove that every word is from God.

00:013:54.000 --> 00:013:57.000
That it is not written by a human being.

00:013:57.000 --> 00:014:00.000
That it is God's message to the world.

00:014:00.000 --> 00:014:05.000
And these mathematically proven statements say

00:014:05.000 --> 00:014:20.000
that our universe with its billion trillion stars, a billion galaxies, 26 billion light year distances is the smallest and innermost of seven universes.

00:014:23.000 --> 00:014:26.000
Can you imagine how big the second universe is

00:014:26.000 --> 00:014:29.000
if our universe is 26 billion light years across?

00:014:29.000 --> 00:014:32.000
T. e second universe, can you imagine how big it is?

00:014:32.000 --> 00:014:34.000
How about the third universe?

00:014:34.000 --> 00:014:37.000
The fourth that is around these?

00:014:37.000 --> 00:014:40.000
You can imagine seven balls inside each other.

00:014:40.000 --> 00:014:45.000
The fifth universe, I don't think we can imagine the size of the fifth universe.

00:014:45.000 --> 00:014:50.000
How about the sixth universe, and the seventh?

00:014:50.000 --> 00:014:59.000
I can tell you right now there is no number in the world that can describe or measure the circumference of the seventh universe.

00:014:59.000 --> 00:015:01.000
Actually the first universe.

00:015:01.000 --> 00:015:04.000
We are the seventh universe, the innermost of the seventh universes.

00:015:04.000 --> 00:015:12.000
There is no number that will describe the circumference of the first universe.

00:015:12.000 --> 00:015:14.000
Now, prepare for another shock.

00:015:14.000 --> 00:015:18.000
Most of you are familiar with that statement in the Quran in Sura 39

00:015:18.000 --> 00:015:27.000
where God says He is holding the seven universes within the fist of His hand.

00:015:27.000 --> 00:015:32.000
In Arabic in the Quran: وَالسَّمَاوَاتُ مَطْوِيَّاتٌ بِيَمِينِهِ

00:015:32.000 --> 00:015:38.000
God is not holding the seven universes like this in two hands.

00:015:38.000 --> 00:015:41.000
God is holding the seven universes in one hand

00:015:41.000 --> 00:015:50.000
and this is allegorical description to give us an idea about the greatness of God and who God is.

00:015:52.000 --> 00:015:58.000
It's an allegorical idea to make us appreciate the greatness of God

00:015:58.000 --> 00:016:16.000
and to make us appreciate and realize the blasphemy of saying that such great God has a human son on the tiny tiny spec called the planet earth.

00:016:16.000 --> 00:016:19.000
I mean how can that be?

00:016:19.000 --> 00:016:29.000
We are a fortunate generation in that with the established scientific facts we can appreciate the greatness of God.

00:016:29.000 --> 00:016:35.000
And God tells us who He is in His message to the world, the Quran.

00:016:35.000 --> 00:016:41.000
And with the sciences we now accomplished, we appreciate that greatness.

00:016:41.000 --> 00:016:51.000
And therefore, we can appreciate the grossness, the blasphemy of saying that God had a wife or a mother or a son.

00:016:51.000 --> 00:017:01.000
We can appreciate, we can realize how blasphemous, how terrible it is to say that God has a partner, another god with Him.

00:017:01.000 --> 00:017:11.000
How can we idolize Muhammad, the tiny human being who existed on a tiny planet called Earth in a tiny solar system.

00:017:11.000 --> 00:017:18.000
What was Muhammad's role in deciding the speed of rotation of the moon, for example?

00:017:18.000 --> 00:017:23.000
The moon rotates around itself and around the Earth.

00:017:23.000 --> 00:017:29.000
Yet, we always see one side of the moon, the same side of the moon

00:017:29.000 --> 00:017:36.000
because of the perfect synchronized movement of the moon around itself and around the Earth,

00:017:36.000 --> 00:017:38.000
we see only one side.

00:017:38.000 --> 00:017:44.000
And if that movement was off by one second, we would see the other side of the moon.

00:017:44.000 --> 00:017:49.000
This precision in God's creation,

00:017:49.000 --> 00:017:57.000
what was the role of Muhammad or Jesus or Mary or Saint Francis in deciding that speed rotation of the moon?

00:017:57.000 --> 00:018:03.000
This elaborate system, everything going in its orbit precisely.

00:018:03.000 --> 00:018:13.000
We know exactly what time the Sun will rise in the year 2025, July 4th, 2025.

00:018:13.000 --> 00:018:22.000
We know exactly in Tucson, Arizona, for example, we know exactly when, what time will the Sun rise and from what spot

00:018:22.000 --> 00:018:28.000
because the Sun follows God's laws, God's creation and follows the exact orbit.

00:018:28.000 --> 00:018:33.000
God is holding the 7 universes in His hand.

00:018:33.000 --> 00:018:38.000
That's who God is.

